---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: author.name,
    section: "Brand Reviews",
    tags: [
      "ritual protein powder",
      "ritual essential protein",
      "ritual protein review",
      "ritual daily shake 18+"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{
    text: "See Our Top Clean Protein Picks",
    link: "/best-clean-protein-powder/",
  }}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Brand Review
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Label-Checked
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Ritual Protein Powder: <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Clean Label, Small Scoop, Big Price</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Ritual built its name on traceable multivitamins, then brought the same pitch to a pea protein shake. Here is what the Daily Shake actually delivers, which version to buy, who should skip it, and what it costs per 25 g of protein.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#ritual-essential-protein-18"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#which-one"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            See the Label Breakdown
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">{author.name}</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">{author.role}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#verdict" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. The Short Verdict</a>
          <a href="#what-ritual-sells" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. What Ritual Actually Sells</a>
          <a href="#label" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. What Is in the Daily Shake</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. The Lineup</a>
          <a href="#which-one" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Which Ritual Protein to Buy</a>
          <a href="#cost" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Cost per 25 g of Protein</a>
          <a href="#testing" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Testing and Certifications</a>
          <a href="#skip" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Who Should Skip Ritual</a>
          <a href="#compare" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. How Ritual Compares</a>
          <a href="#using" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Getting the Most From It</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">12. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Ritual's Essential Protein Daily Shake is a tidy, well-documented pea protein with a short ingredient list and real third-party paperwork behind it. It is also a 20 g scoop sold at a price that works out to roughly three to four dollars per 25 g of protein. Buy it for the label and the testing, not for value.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="verdict" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The Short Verdict
          </h2>

          <p>
            Ritual's protein is good at what it sets out to do and expensive for what it delivers. The Daily Shake gives you 20 g of organic pea protein in about 120 calories per the vanilla label, with zero grams of sugar, a few grams of fat from coconut MCT oil and a short ingredient list you can read in ten seconds. Ritual backs that with an unusual stack of paperwork for a plant protein, including a Clean Label Project Purity Award and NSF Contents Certification on its current product pages. If those things are why you are shopping, it is a reasonable buy.
          </p>

          <p>
            The problem is the dose and the price together. A 20 g serving is on the small side for a protein shake, and at Ritual's list price of about 44 dollars for 15 servings, you are paying close to three dollars per scoop before any discount. Scale that to a 25 g dose and the cost lands somewhere between about 2.90 and 4.20 dollars depending on whether you subscribe, buy one bag direct, or buy from a retailer. Mainstream pea and whey proteins regularly come in at half that or less.
          </p>

          <p>
            So the honest answer to whether Ritual protein is any good is yes, with a narrow audience. It suits a buyer who wants a dairy-free shake with an easy-to-verify label, who is already in Ritual's subscription for vitamins, or who is pregnant or postpartum and wants the version with extra choline. It does not suit someone trying to hit a high daily protein target on a budget, or a lifter who wants 30 g in one scoop.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">THE VERDICT</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">A clean, documented pea shake priced like a premium whey isolate.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">Buy the standard Daily Shake if label transparency and testing matter more to you than cost per gram. Buy the Pregnancy and Postpartum version only if you specifically want the higher choline. Everyone else gets more protein per dollar from the alternatives below.</p>
          </div>

          <p>
            Everything that follows is built on Ritual's own published labels, retailer supplement panels and the certification bodies' public claims. We have not tasted or lab-tested the product ourselves, and where we mention taste or mixing it is buyer feedback reported as such. If you want the wider field of low-contaminant powders this one competes with, our <a href="/best-clean-protein-powder/">best clean protein powder</a> guide ranks the category on testing first.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="what-ritual-sells" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. What Ritual Actually Sells
          </h2>

          <p>
            Ritual is best known as a subscription vitamin company. Its multivitamins were the brand's first products, and its whole pitch is traceability: it names where its ingredients come from and publishes how they are tested. The brand entered the protein category in 2021, when it launched Essential Protein in three versions, labelled 18+, 50+ and Pregnancy and Postpartum, according to trade coverage from NutraIngredients at the time. Ritual is also a Certified B Corporation, which it displays on its protein pages.
          </p>

          <p>
            The protein range today is smaller than that launch line-up. At the time of writing, Ritual's site sells the Essential Protein Daily Shake in Vanilla and Chocolate, and a separate Essential Protein Daily Shake for Pregnancy and Postpartum in Vanilla. The product page that used to hold the 50+ shake now loads the standard Daily Shake, which suggests the 50+ formula has been folded into the main product. If you see a 50+ bag in a retailer listing, check the date and the panel, because the older 50+ formula listed calcium HMB and more calcium, and we could not confirm it is still being made.
          </p>

          <p>
            Naming is a little messy, which matters when you shop. Ritual's own pages use both Daily Shake and Essential Protein for the same product, and retailers still list it as Daily Shake 18+. Amazon lists the vanilla bag under a more generic title along the lines of Ritual Vegan Pea Protein Powder, Vanilla, 1 lb. These are all the same core product: a 15-serving bag of pea protein with about 20 g per serving.
          </p>

          <p>
            Ritual sells mostly direct, with a membership model. Its product pages show a regular price, a lower subscriber price and a higher one-time price for non-members with shipping added. Vitacost, Grove and Amazon carry the vanilla Daily Shake as well, typically at or near the full list price. The chocolate flavor and the pregnancy version are easier to find on Ritual's own site than on Amazon, where we could only confirm the vanilla Daily Shake listing at the time of writing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="label" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. What Is in the Daily Shake
          </h2>

          <p>
            The vanilla Daily Shake panel, as listed by Vitacost at the time of writing, reads like this: a serving of 5 tablespoons, or about a third of a cup, weighing roughly 30 g, with 120 calories, 3 g of fat, 3 g of carbohydrate including 2 g of fiber, 0 g of sugar and 20 g of protein. There are 15 servings per bag. Ritual's chocolate page lists the same 20 g of protein in a slightly larger 31 g serving at 130 calories, which is what the cocoa adds.
          </p>

          <p>
            The protein is organic pea protein, which Ritual says comes from North American peas. Pea protein on its own is low in methionine, one of the essential amino acids, so Ritual adds 400 mg of L-methionine per serving to round out the profile. That is a sensible fix rather than a gimmick, and it is why Ritual can describe the shake as a complete protein. The vanilla panel lists about 1.8 g of leucine per serving, the amino acid most closely linked with triggering muscle protein synthesis.
          </p>

          <p>
            The rest of the ingredient list is short: natural flavor, xanthan gum for thickness, coconut MCT oil, salt, sunflower lecithin to help it mix, mixed tocopherols as an antioxidant, and the sweeteners. Ritual also adds 150 mg of choline per serving in the standard shake. Sodium is higher than many people expect, at 290 mg per serving on the vanilla panel, so if you are watching salt that is worth knowing.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The sweeteners differ by flavor</h3>

          <p>
            This is the detail most reviews skip. The vanilla Daily Shake is sweetened with rebaudioside M, a stevia-derived sweetener Ritual describes as made from fermented sugarcane, plus monk fruit extract. The chocolate page lists monk fruit extract alone and states the product contains no stevia. If stevia aftertaste bothers you, chocolate is the one to try. Neither flavor uses sucralose, sugar alcohols or added sugar, per the labels at the time of writing.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
