        <div id="which-one" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Which Ritual Protein to Buy
          </h2>

          <p>
            For almost everyone, the answer is the standard Daily Shake. It has the same 20 g of pea protein as the pregnancy version, the same base ingredients and the same certifications on Ritual's pages, and it comes in two flavors instead of one. Pick vanilla if you want the Amazon listing or a neutral base for smoothies, and chocolate if you want to avoid stevia-derived sweeteners or plan to drink it with milk.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Pregnancy and Postpartum shake is the same idea with more choline. Its label lists 250 mg of choline per serving, compared with 150 mg in the standard shake, and slightly less sodium, at 210 mg. Choline needs rise during pregnancy and breastfeeding, and many prenatal vitamins carry little of it, which is the gap Ritual is targeting. That is a legitimate reason to choose it, but it is still a 20 g pea shake, and it is not a substitute for a prenatal vitamin or medical advice.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you are pregnant, breastfeeding, managing a kidney condition or taking medication, talk to your doctor or a registered dietitian before adding any protein powder, including this one. Ritual's testing claims are reassuring, but the right total protein and choline intake for you depends on your diet and health, and that is a conversation for a clinician rather than a product page.
          </p>

          <p>
            Skip any listing still sold as the 50+ shake unless you can confirm it is fresh stock. At the time of writing, the 50+ product page on Ritual's site redirects to the standard shake, so a 50+ bag on a marketplace could be old inventory. Older adults are well served by the standard Daily Shake, though most will benefit from a bigger serving or a second protein source in the same meal, because protein needs per meal tend to rise with age.
          </p>

          <p>
            Finally, if you came to Ritual for a high-protein shake rather than for its label story, the Ritual range is probably the wrong place to start. Both alternatives in the lineup below deliver more protein per scoop, and one of them costs a fraction as much per gram.
          </p>
